<%# The self-submit-to-OmniAuth frame (extracted from sessions/start.html.erb
    by story 0021). OmniAuth's request phase is POST-only, and two callers
    need to turn a GET into that POST: the auth sheet (`ASWebAuthenticationSession`
    can only open a URL) and the dev-only mock sign-in door (a human clicking
    a button). One definition, so a future change to the CSRF handling or the
    markup can't drift between two copies.

    `url:` is the only local — everything else about the frame is identical
    between callers. No layout: this frame exists for milliseconds and must
    not pull the masthead, the compass or the corner into it.

    `<noscript>` carries a real button — better a control than a dead end. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Signing in — Tondo</title>
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <style>
      html, body { height: 100%; margin: 0; background: #f4efe6; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <%= form_with url: url, method: :post, id: "start", data: { turbo: false } do |f| %>
      <noscript><%= f.submit "Continue" %></noscript>
    <% end %>
    <script>document.getElementById("start").submit();</script>
  </body>
</html>
